-- arm 3b: does a NAME resolve to what an ATTRIBUTE does? ------
        by name     : /nix/store/7g3xfllgmf6ndlpgdv63l0p8pbadk3fv-gawk-5.4.1
        by attribute: ny5hzk3l36pldfsjkh56ia7y55xr23vd-gawk-5.4.1
  ok    the name and the attribute name the same store path = different
        ⛔ They differ, and there are TWO reasons, both real:
          1. CHANNEL SKEW. The index is one channel snapshot; the nix on
             this machine has another. Same package, different revision,
             different store path -- which is what 'gawk' shows here.
          2. THE ATTRIBUTE IS NOT THE NAME. nixpkgs' 'bash' attribute is
             bash-interactive, and no name match can know that.
          Either way an index lookup is not an evaluation, and a plan must
          record which route produced it. Both do.

